      "function": "fuzz_parse_http_request",
      "line": 1659,
      "code": "if (parse_http_request(&request) == HTTP_OK) {",
      "note": "The exact 34-byte witness contains `\\r\\n\\r\\n`, so `read_request_finalizer()` returns `FINALIZER_DONE`. In `identify_http_path()`, `space = end_of_line - sizeof(\"HTTP/X.X\")` lands on byte `0xb9`; after `*space++ = '\\0'`, the version switch sees `HTTP/1.1`, `url_decode(request->url.value)` safely decodes only the path `/%64T /`, and `parse_http_request(&request)` returns `HTTP_OK`. The saved crashing path therefore reaches `parse_query_string(&request)` at line 1664.",
      "oracle_kind": "gt_parser_checkpoint",
      "kind": "parser_admitted"
    },
    {
      "file": "src/lib/lwan-request.c",
      "function": "identify_http_path",
      "line": 484,
      "code": "end_of_line = memchr(buffer, '\\r', helper->buffer->len - (size_t)end_len);\n*end_of_line = '\\0';\nspace = end_of_line - sizeof(\"HTTP/X.X\");",
      "note": "This derived `space` pointer is the vulnerability-relevant parser state consumed immediately to size `request->url`, later to size `helper->query_string`, and then overwritten so the malformed line still passes the HTTP version check.",
      "kind": "source"
    },
    {
      "file": "src/lib/lwan-request.c",
      "function": "decode_hex_digit",
      "line": null,
      "code": "return hex_digit_tbl[(unsigned int)ch];",
      "note": "On the witnessed call, `url_decode()` passes `ch[2] == (char)0xdb` from the query key. Because `char` is signed on this build, integer promotion sign-extends that byte before the cast to `unsigned int`, so the index is not constrained to `[0,255]`. The staged patch fixes this exact obligation by changing the cast to `unsigned char`.",
      "kind": "root_cause_function"
    },
